# Keep the build context to what the image actually needs: src/ and the two
# requirements files. Everything else here is either useless in the image or
# actively harmful in it.
#
# .venv is the harmful one. It is a macOS-arm64 virtualenv built by
# scripts/create-venv.sh; copied into a Linux image it would be several hundred
# megabytes of unusable binaries, and its site-packages would sit on the same
# PYTHONPATH as the one the builder stage produces.
#
# .git is not listed because the context root is app/, which contains no .git.
# The repository's .git is one level up and never enters the context.

.venv
tests
dist
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.coverage
.env
docker-compose.yml
README.md

# The **/ prefix is load-bearing, and its absence was a real defect.
#
# .dockerignore patterns are anchored to the context root, so a bare
# `__pycache__` excludes only app/__pycache__ — never app/src/bgd/__pycache__.
# Without these two lines the image shipped 24 host-compiled .pyc files, and the
# image digest changed every time someone ran `make test`, because that is what
# regenerates them. The entries above are all context-root paths, so they need
# no prefix; these two are nested and do.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
